<title>USA: MicroTouch says to pay arbitration costs.</title>
<headline>MicroTouch says to pay arbitration costs.</headline>
<dateline>METHUEN, Mass. 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>MicroTouch Systems Inc said Monday an abitrator ruled the company must pay $595,000 in a dispute with its former Japanese distributor, Nissha Printing Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The company said the award is considerably less than the maximum exposure of nearly $2 million it had anticipated.</p>
<p>MicroTouch said it will recognize the costs as a one-time charge in its second quarter 1997 financial statements.</p>
<p>MicroTouch said the award includes a $300,000 contribution toward the legal costs incurred by Nissha and $295,000 of International Chamber of Commerce administrative fees.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
